            "url": "https://generesolve.io/fhir/StructureDefinition/etiology-classification",
            "valueString": "single_gene — The patient presents with a constellation of symptoms including kidney failure, burning limb pain, abdominal pain, intolerance to temperature extremes, hypertension, and hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, along with a family history suggestive of an inherited disorder affecting multiple systems.. The combination of symptoms affecting multiple organ systems (kidneys, nerves, heart) and the presence of similar symptoms in family members (daughter, maternal cousin) strongly suggests a single genetic defect causing a systemic disorder. The specific symptoms point towards conditions like Fabry disease or mitochondrial disorders, which are typically inherited in a single-gene manner"
